    "text": "FOX Reno\nwebsite\nNevada\nRegional leaders discuss future regulations on construction of data centers\nBy Will Payne,\n2 hours agoMore than 40 of them already, with several others in the works.... The data center boom in Nevada is real, and it makes sense. An abundance of land, tax incentives, and the availability of clean, cost-effective energy are just a few reasons why corporations like Apple, Google, and Amazon have decided to house critical IT infrastructure and computer servers here in the Silver State.",
